expectation e_susumu_portable_project_memory target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Susumu keeps portable project memory" detail="Susumu should preserve observed evidence, authored expectations, verification results, decisions, and work records in portable artifacts that can be reviewed outside the original source tree.";
expectation e_susumu_scanner_truth_boundary target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Scanner evidence remains distinct from judgment" detail="Susumu should keep scanner-observed facts, deterministic derived findings, human intent, verification reports, decisions, work records, and optional AI drafts visibly separate.";
expectation e_susumu_review_packets target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Review packets are useful standalone artifacts" detail="Susumu should create review packets that include enough artifact, review, source-preview, and next-action context for engineers, stakeholders, and agents to inspect later.";
expectation e_susumu_ci_pr_artifacts target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Pull requests can produce Susumu review artifacts" detail="The repository should demonstrate how CI can generate machine-readable check output, review packets, and standalone HTML review portals for pull requests.";
expectation e_susumu_pages_portal target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Main branch publishes the latest Susumu portal" detail="The repository should demonstrate how the latest Susumu review portal can be published as an always-current static site from CI, using GitHub Pages for open source and the same artifact pattern for internal business portals.";
expectation e_susumu_ai_optional target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="AI assistance stays optional and labeled" detail="Susumu should not require AI keys for core scanning, checking, review packets, or portal export. Optional AI output should be labeled, cited, and reviewable before becoming trusted project memory.";
expectation e_susumu_repo_init target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Projects can start the Susumu way" detail="Susumu should provide a simple repository initialization flow that creates an authored expectations sidecar without requiring users to hand-write the artifact syntax first.";
expectation e_susumu_auto_expectations target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Initialized projects load expectations automatically" detail="When scanning a repository directory, Susumu should automatically merge the repository's expectations.susu sidecar when no explicit expectations file is supplied, so initialized projects follow the Susumu workflow by default.";
expectation e_susumu_review_build target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Daily review builds run in one command" detail="Susumu should provide a single review build command that scans the project, writes the current artifact, records machine-readable check output when requested, creates a review packet, and optionally exports or serves the review portal.";
expectation e_susumu_expectation_support target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Expectations show their supporting evidence" detail="Susumu review packets should summarize each expectation's current support, including whether its target is observed, which verification statuses exist, how much work or decision context is linked, and which gaps remain.";
expectation e_susumu_git_work_support target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Git work can support project expectations" detail="Susumu should be able to connect local Git commits to project-level expectations and export work records from those commits, so expectation support can reflect real repository activity without hand-authored work records.";
expectation e_susumu_easy_daily_cli target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Daily Susumu commands stay simple" detail="Susumu should make normal project review workflows easy to remember and type, using short commands like review, status, open, and git with convention-based files while preserving advanced options for detailed control.";
expectation e_susumu_docs_teach_daily_workflow target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Documentation teaches the daily Susumu workflow" detail="Susumu documentation should introduce the simple human workflow first, explain which files people author and which files Susumu generates, and keep advanced commands discoverable without making them the default path.";
expectation e_susumu_explicit_git_links target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Commits can be explicitly linked to expectations" detail="When Susumu cannot safely infer which expectation a commit supports, users should be able to explicitly link that commit to an expectation and write a work record without rewriting Git history.";
expectation e_susumu_git_suggests_next_links target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Git connection output suggests next links" detail="When Susumu reports unconnected commits, the output should suggest concrete next commands and likely expectation candidates so users can continue the daily workflow without guessing the syntax.";
expectation e_susumu_expectations_are_easy_to_browse target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Expectations are easy to browse and choose" detail="Susumu should provide a simple daily command for listing, searching, and filtering expectation ids so users can quickly choose the right expectation for git links, reviews, and verification work.";
expectation e_susumu_verify_is_easy target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Expectations are easy to verify" detail="Susumu should provide a simple daily command for recording passed, failed, or inconclusive verification evidence against an expectation, so support can become explicit reviewable proof without hand-writing syntax.";
expectation e_susumu_git_link_preserves_multiple_expectations target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Explicit Git links preserve multiple expectations" detail="When a user links the same commit to multiple expectations, Susumu should create stable expectation-specific work records instead of overwriting an earlier link for that commit.";
expectation e_susumu_portal_expectation_ladder target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Portal shows each expectation's evidence ladder" detail="Susumu's review portal should make each expectation's evidence ladder clear, showing observed target evidence, linked work, verification evidence, decision context, review status, and the next suggested action.";
expectation e_susumu_portal_readiness_board target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Portal summarizes expectation readiness" detail="Susumu's review portal should group expectations by readiness so stakeholders can quickly see which expectations are verified, need verification, need linked work, have failed checks, or have missing targets.";
expectation e_susumu_portal_dirty_source_links target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Portal links dirty records to source evidence" detail="Susumu's review portal should surface dirty or stale evidence flags and show nearby syntax-highlighted source when a record or finding has a file location.";
expectation e_susumu_portal_traceability_scroll target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Traceability panes scroll independently" detail="The review portal's traceability page should let users scroll the expectation list and selected evidence detail independently so long expectation lists do not block inspection of the right-hand evidence pane.";
expectation e_susumu_portal_calm_contained_theme target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Portal uses a calm contained default theme" detail="The review portal should use soft, low-glare default colors and keep traceability detail content contained within its card so long ids, code previews, or evidence text do not break the layout.";
expectation e_susumu_portal_brand_config target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Portal branding can be configured" detail="Susumu should let projects brand the generated portal with local configuration for colors, names, and related visual identity without changing the review packet's evidence semantics.";
expectation e_susumu_git_exports_multiple_expectations target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Git work can support multiple expectations" detail="When one commit deterministically supports multiple expectations, Susumu should export separate work records so each expectation receives explicit work support instead of collapsing the commit to a single expectation.";
expectation e_susumu_packet_readiness_queue target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Review packets expose expectation readiness" detail="Susumu review packets should include a machine-readable expectation readiness queue so agents, CI, and portal users can rely on the same readiness buckets and next actions.";
expectation e_susumu_readiness_command target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Readiness is easy to inspect from the CLI" detail="Susumu should provide a simple readiness command that reads the latest review packet and prints expectation readiness counts and next actions, with JSON output for agents and CI.";
expectation e_susumu_readiness_filters target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Readiness can be filtered quickly" detail="Susumu readiness output should support bucket and text filters so humans, agents, and CI can quickly focus on failed, unverified, unsupported, or topic-specific expectations.";
expectation e_susumu_infrastructure_work_kind target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Work records can describe infrastructure changes" detail="Susumu work records should include an infrastructure kind so CI, deployment, hosting, and configuration changes do not have to be mislabeled as implementation or other work.";
expectation e_susumu_modular_cli target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="CLI implementation grows through focused modules" detail="Susumu should keep the command-line surface easy to extend by moving cohesive parsing, routing, and command support code out of the monolithic binary entry point into focused modules with regression coverage.";
expectation e_susumu_compliance_support_stays_honest target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Compliance support stays evidence-oriented and non-certifying" detail="Susumu may help development teams and businesses assemble, inspect, and preserve evidence toward their own compliance processes, but Susumu must never state or imply that a control, regulation, certification, or compliance requirement has been met or will be met. Human and organizational review remain authoritative.";
expectation e_susumu_verification_history_is_append_only target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Verification history is append-only" detail="Supported Susumu commands must preserve prior verification records and represent replacement or retraction as a new record linked to the prior record, while remaining explicit that direct edits to ordinary text files require a later tamper-evidence layer.";
expectation e_susumu_evidence_hashes_are_provider_neutral target=project subject=- status=accepted source="human:maintainer" title="Evidence hashes are provider-neutral and privacy-safe" detail="Susumu should be able to record a content hash for an evidence artifact supplied by any local or CI/CD environment without uploading or copying the artifact contents, while clearly stating that a hash alone does not prove execution, provenance, retention, or compliance.";
